      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "75. Milk, at first, imparted all (its) qualities to its consti-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tuent water; on seeing the distress of milk (i. e. when it was",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "heated ) water sacrificed itself in the fire ( i. e. became evapo-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "rated ); seeing the distress of its friend ( i. e. water ), it ( viz.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "milk ) became very eager to throw itself into the fire ( lit. to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "go to the fire, i. e. began to boil over ); but it settled down",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "when united with that water--such is the friendship of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "the good.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "76. In one part sleeps Kes'ava; in another is the host of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "his foes; in a third the chain of mountains seeking shelter; in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "another part yet is Vàḍava ( submarine ) fire with all the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "world-destroying fires. Oh, how extensive, deep and endur-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ing is the expanse of the sea !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "77. Cut down ( check ) desire, have recourse to patience,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "give up pride, fix not ( your ) attachment on sinful deeds,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "speak the truth, follow the footsteps of the good, serve the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "learned, reverence those that deserve respect, conciliate",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "( your ) enemies, do not parade your good qualities, preserve",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "fame and sympathise with those in ditress; this is the charac-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "teristic of the good.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
